# ONE ordered name/value list builds the record, for both writers below. The earlier form spelled
# every field twice — once as a `--arg` flag, once in a printf format string — in two lists nothing
# kept in agreement; this probe has since tripled the field count, which would have tripled that
# hazard. Adding a field here now reaches both paths by construction.
#
# The first 21 entries are the v1 field names, unchanged and in their original order:
# packages/results/src/lib/specs.ts joins this record onto ObservedSpecs by those exact keys, so
# renaming or nesting one silently blanks a leaderboard column for every future run.
RECORD_FIELDS=(
	public_ip "$PUBLIC_IP"
	org "$ORG"
	asn "$ASN"
	org_name "$ORG_NAME"
	reverse_dns "$HOSTNAME_PTR"
	city "$CITY"
	region "$REGION"
	country "$COUNTRY"
	loc "$LOC"
	timezone "$TIMEZONE"
	manufacturer "$MANUFACTURER"
	product_name "$PRODUCT_NAME"
